When `hideEmpty` filters out fields, the section header’s field-count Badge still uses `section.fields.length` (original count) elsewhere in this component, which will become inaccurate. Consider switching the count display to use the filtered `visibleFields.length` when `hideEmpty` is enabled.
```suggestion

  // When hideEmpty is enabled, ensure any field-count display based on
  // section.fields.length reflects the filtered set of visible fields.
  if (section.hideEmpty && section.fields !== visibleFields) {
    section.fields = visibleFields;
  }
```

Same issue as EmailCellRenderer: `navigator.clipboard.writeText(...)` is called without checking `navigator.clipboard` exists, so it can throw in insecure contexts before `.catch()` runs. Guard before calling.
```suggestion
    try {
      const clipboard = navigator.clipboard;
      if (!clipboard || typeof clipboard.writeText !== 'function') {
        // Clipboard API is not available in this context
        return;
      }
      clipboard
        .writeText(String(value))
        .then(() => {
          setCopied(true);
          setTimeout(() => setCopied(false), 2000);
        })
        .catch(() => {
          // Clipboard write failed
        });
    } catch {
      // Accessing navigator.clipboard is not allowed in this context
    }
```

This assertion relies on internal styling/classnames (`.border-b .rounded-full`) to locate header badges, which is brittle against styling refactors. Since badges already have `aria-label` in the implementation, prefer querying by accessible name/role (or a testid) scoped to the header.
```suggestion
    render(<DetailView schema={schema} />);
    // The header area should have a badge for the non-empty status but not for the empty department
    const statusBadge = screen.getByLabelText('Status: Active');
    expect(statusBadge).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.queryByLabelText(/Department:/i)).toBeNull();
```

`handleCopy` calls `navigator.clipboard.writeText(...)` without guarding for `navigator.clipboard` being undefined. In insecure contexts or older browsers this throws before the Promise `.catch()` runs. Add an existence check or wrap the call in try/catch before attempting to write.
```suggestion

    if (typeof navigator === 'undefined' || !navigator.clipboard || typeof navigator.clipboard.writeText !== 'function') {
      // Clipboard API is not available in this environment
      return;
    }

    try {
      navigator.clipboard
        .writeText(String(value))
        .then(() => {
          setCopied(true);
          setTimeout(() => setCopied(false), 2000);
        })
        .catch(() => {
          // Clipboard write failed or is not permitted
        });
    } catch {
      // Accessing navigator.clipboard or calling writeText threw synchronously
    }
```

Header title uses `(schema.primaryField && data?.[schema.primaryField]) || ...`, which treats valid falsy values (e.g. 0/false) as “empty” and incorrectly falls back to `schema.title`. Prefer an explicit emptiness check (null/undefined/empty string) before falling back.
```suggestion
                {(() => {
                  const primaryFieldValue = schema.primaryField ? data?.[schema.primaryField] : undefined;
                  const hasPrimaryFieldValue =
                    primaryFieldValue !== null &&
                    primaryFieldValue !== undefined &&
                    primaryFieldValue !== '';
                  const headerTitle =
                    (hasPrimaryFieldValue ? String(primaryFieldValue) : undefined) ??
                    schema.title ??
                    'Details';
                  return (
                    <h1 className="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold truncate">
                      {headerTitle}
                    </h1>
                  );
                })()}
```
